# Template for `.dev.vars` — local secrets consumed by the Wrangler/Vite dev
# runtime (Cloudflare Workers env vars for local dev, NOT `.env`/Vite client
# vars). `.dev.vars*` is gitignored except this example file.
#
# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` and fill in real values before running
# `bun run dev`:
#
#   cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars

# Session signing secret, at least 32 characters. Make one with
# `openssl rand -hex 32` (64 characters) and paste it over the placeholder,
# which is too short on purpose so a build outside dev refuses it.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=paste-openssl-rand-hex-32

# Better Auth base URL: the origin the app is served from. Auth links, the
# origin check and Secure cookies all hang off it.
# - A dev build (`bun run dev`) follows each request's own origin, so you can
#   leave this unset. It also falls back to a dev-only secret when
#   BETTER_AUTH_SECRET is unset.
# - Any other build (preview, staging, production, or `bun run preview`
#   locally) never trusts the request's Host: every request fails with a 500
#   unless BETTER_AUTH_URL is set and BETTER_AUTH_SECRET is at least 32
#   characters (and not the dev-only fallback). BETTER_AUTH_URL must be
#   https://, or http://localhost / http://127.0.0.1 with any port.
#   Deployed environments set both per env in wrangler (a var for the URL,
#   `wrangler secret put` for the secret).
# An https:// URL turns on Secure, __Secure- prefixed session cookies.
# Running a production build locally (`bun run preview` serves on 4173):
# BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:4173

# Optional — extra origins allowed to send cookie-carrying requests to the
# auth API (the base URL's own origin is always trusted). Comma-separated.
# - An exact entry is a bare origin: https://admin.example.com
# - A wildcard entry is https:// (http:// only in a dev build), then a host
#   that starts with `*.` or `*-` followed by a domain you own of at least
#   two labels. The `*` is the only one and matches any run of characters.
#   A bare shared suffix (`*.workers.dev`, `*.pages.dev`) is refused. Workers
#   per-PR previews: https://*-<worker>-preview.<subdomain>.workers.dev
# AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS=https://admin.example.com,https://*-my-app-preview.my-team.workers.dev

# Optional — OTLP trace export.
# Unset = tracing export off (logs still carry traceId). Local viewer:
# `otel-tui` or Jaeger listen on http://localhost:4318.
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318
# OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS=Authorization=Bearer%20<token>
# OTEL_SERVICE_NAME=cf-saas-starter

# Optional — server-side analytics. ANALYTICS_PROVIDER: none (default) | console | posthog.
# ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=posthog
# POSTHOG_API_KEY=phc_...
# POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com

# Optional — error reporting (docs/agents/error-reporting.md).
# ERROR_REPORTER: console (default) | none | sentry. With sentry and no usable
# SENTRY_DSN the reporter falls back to console.
# ERROR_REPORTER=sentry
# SENTRY_DSN=https://abc123@o0.ingest.example.com/1
# RELEASE_VERSION=unversioned
# ENVIRONMENT=development

# Optional — sampling. The preset for ENVIRONMENT sets the rates
# (docs/agents/logging.md); these override it. A number from 0 to 1.
# Warnings, errors and the spans of a failed request are always kept.
# LOG_SAMPLE_RATE=1
# TRACE_SAMPLE_RATE=0.1
